+  <header class="hero">
+    <p class="eyebrow">Pull request explainer · COR-1185</p>
+    <h1>A durable handoff for mirror creation</h1>
+    <p class="dek">This pull request teaches the CLI to submit mirror creation as a persistent server-side request, poll that request until placement exists, and then reuse the existing clone-readiness poll. The old synchronous route remains the default while the new route rolls out.</p>
+    <div class="meta">
+      <span class="pill">PR #2207</span>
+      <span class="pill">21 changed files</span>
+      <span class="pill">7 reviewable commits</span>
+      <span class="pill">Default-off rollout</span>
+    </div>
+  </header>
+
+  <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
+    <a href="#background"><b>01 · Background</b><span>Why a long HTTP request is a fragile ownership boundary.</span></a>
+    <a href="#intuition"><b>02 · Intuition</b><span>The receipt-and-poll model, with concrete examples.</span></a>
+    <a href="#code"><b>03 · Code</b><span>How routing, polling, settings, and callers fit together.</span></a>
